        "original_id": "5246e377-2dcb-5dfe-b7be-02bdea2c2a8c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Dudman\n- Places: King's College, Taunton; University of Hull; Lincoln Theological College; Shiregreen; Wombwell; Frodingham; Lincolnshire; Scunthorpe; North Lincolnshire\n- Roles: curacies; Industrial Chaplain to the Bishop of Lincoln\n\nFacts:\n- Bill Dudman was educated at King's College, Taunton, the University of Hull, and Lincoln Theological College.\n- Bill Dudman served curacies at Shiregreen, Wombwell, and Frodingham before 1957.\n- From 1957 to 1971, Bill Dudman was Industrial Chaplain to the Bishop of Lincoln.\n- Frodingham was a hamlet in Lincolnshire.\n- Frodingham later grew into a suburb of Scunthorpe in North Lincolnshire.",
